      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CH'IEN Wei-ch'êng 錢維城 (T. 宗磐, 幼安, H. 稼軒, 茶山), 1720–1772, official and artist, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangsu. Having taken his chü-jên degree at the age of nineteen sui (1738), he was four years later (1742) appointed a secretary in the Grand Secretariat—after passing a special examination.",
